id: pm-swarm-durable-close-recovery
title: Durable multi-item close recovery
description: "Durable native close recovery on one shared tracker: registered field intent, immutable member restore targets, native phase receipts, guarded success metadata cleanup, and idempotent reverse compensation. Pending recovery precedes terminal and owner guards; unowned or superseded state is preserved. Verification and orchestrator closure remain separate."
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: close-recovery,durability,"gh:unbraind/pm-swarm#34","gh:unbraind/pm-swarm#65"
created_at: "2026-10-27T19:53:07.216Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-10T12:15:15.326Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Canonicalize short IDs through host native get before every history read, including service-capable contexts; capture history heads before authoritative decision documents and recheck under the same native writer lock; identify own forward close and every restore by a durable unique compensation_id and exact SDK journal identity, never author, message markers or document equality; refuse unrelated same-author native closes and copied transaction markers; native close owns dependent unblock, blocker-field removal, Plan behavior and unchanged warnings, and actual read-back defines successors; persist full immutable member/pre-close bytes digest/post-close history domain before restore, fsync intent, progress and parent-directory updates; durable per-member restored/pending receipts recover own progress without mistaking it for peers; never restore peers or foreign records, and release/claim/restore ABA must be detected from locked native history heads even when all bytes and tokens match; real-process SIGKILL after every forward and reverse step including 0..N member restores with 1-3 dependents converges to exact pre-close item bytes with append-only audit history, no duplicates or loss; peer edits between restores stop with typed partial receipts preserving restored and pending members; lost native returns and ordinary coordinator failures preserve all lifecycle members coherently; packed npm/Bun, non-Git and installed separate/shared SDK layouts exercise every boundary; property tests, revert proofs, full 100 percent coverage, documentation and release gates."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-swarm-y972,related,"2026-10-27T19:53:07.216Z",codex-agent,"cli:create:dep",detected
comments[85]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T20:23:51.975Z",codex-agent,"Repository issue https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/issues/34 owns the full rounds 5-15 close protocol. It is related to pm-swarm-y972; the existing dependent-progress issue 32 is linked as a narrower subtask. Removed prototype and tests remain reproducible from commit 0157465. Current PR intentionally has no swarm close transaction, automatic primary restore, member compensation, native-history ownership reconstruction or saved-result adoption."
  "2026-10-27T21:15:24.658Z",codex-agent,"Scope boundary implemented in PR 24: fresh native close only, immutable refusal after lost returns, prior native closes or legacy markers. Current regressions preserve an unrelated same-author close, service-context short IDs, reopened preimages and native dependent effects after SIGKILL. Full journaled recovery, exact compensation ownership and all multi-member restore progress remain this open Feature and issue 34. No automatic restore implementation ships."
  "2026-11-02T09:18:35.763Z",pi-glm,"Triage 2026-11-02 (missed-watch sweep): still valid, tracked here (gh:unbraind/pm-swarm#34). The deferred durable multi-item close recovery protocol (rounds 5-15 acceptance: identity-bound restores, immutable member lists and digests, fsynced progress, SIGKILL resume, peer-edit refusal) is not implemented on main; PR #24 deliberately reduced close to fresh native delegation. The narrower member-progress subtask remains pm-swarm-durable-compensation (gh:unbraind/pm-swarm#32). No duplicate item created."
  "2026-11-06T09:12:58.095Z",codex-sol,"Read the complete linked issues and current implementation. Verify the existing handoff successor guard with real processes; implement native-history-bound durable close intent and per-member recovery through the pinned SDK, with crash and peer-interleaving regressions. No SDK dependency bump or release workflow change planned."
  "2026-11-06T09:37:15.767Z",codex-sol,"Native close still owns dependent selection, Plan policy, blocker cleanup and warning tokens. The protocol records a unique SDK-validated compensation identity in native-field intent and derives native episode identities from exact phase/member targets. It compensates interrupted forward prefixes rather than replaying close on a terminal primary. Dependents restore first, with certified lost-progress recovery; final primary restore locks restored dependents while checking the domain. Complete-byte restoration retains all native audit events. README, ARCHITECTURE and native-close documentation describe the state machine."
  "2026-11-06T09:59:09.434Z",codex-sol,"Storage/lease-tail fault enumeration passed 156/156 checks, including 130 observed-operation injections. A failed final lease cleanup exposed a replay deadlock behind its still-live pin; completed native receipts now replay read-only before lease acquisition. Expanded crash diagnostics include native intent, journal and restore commits before fsync/return, plus durable boundaries. Packed npm/Bun crash coverage is isolated from command smoke tests and removes only its verified synthetic completed members between cases to bound corpus cost; the first growing-fixture packed attempt timed out and is not acceptance evidence."
  "2026-11-06T10:26:22.624Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral reverts in disposable copies: original completeClaim produced 45 failing regressions out of 46 (the independent missing-restore guard is separately tested); reverting final handoff cleanup failed 2/2 process scenarios; disabling member resume failed 3/3; weakening ownership history proof failed 3/3; removing final dependency locks failed its real-peer test; removing intent validation failed its persisted-intent test. Restored implementation passed 24/24 focused tests. Additional missing-receipt, Plan and fsync revert controls are running. Isolated packed npm/Bun consumers passed 2/2 acceptance tests, covering 24 real SIGKILL cases. Native Plan closure also matches an independently cloned native SDK oracle."
  "2026-11-06T11:01:03.376Z",codex-sol,"Pre-gate adversarial review found a real ownership gap: copying the global close episode onto an untouched admitted member could make a peer edit look like an owned forward mutation. A new real-process regression failed before the correction. The native admission hook now signs each exact target, operation, before-head and before/after document hashes under its native item lock, using an ephemeral Ed25519 key. The public key is anchored in registered intent; signed proposals are durably staged by the same host SDK in audited workspace settings before the item write, then frozen into native item history before compensation. The private key is never serialized. Copied episodes and same-author native closes now lack the required signed proposal and are preserved with typed partial receipts. The corrected regression passes; fresh signed-protocol focused tests passed 11/11. Earlier gates and revert proofs are interim evidence and will be refreshed for this design."
  "2026-11-06T11:07:53.705Z",codex-sol,"The signed-proposal design is now exercised through the pinned pm runner: its eight linked real-tracker regressions passed with the updated timeout. Exact signed proposals also bind unlogged bytes and native SDK history; a copied episode on an untouched member no longer authorizes rollback. Pending compensation validates its complete frozen post-close heads before any restore. Current signature, history-outage, Plan-policy and privacy checks are being measured before the full npm/Bun gates; no claim of final coverage or CI is made yet."
  "2026-11-06T11:36:09.072Z",codex-sol,"Signed-protocol behavioral reverts in disposable copies are complete: original close failed 56 of 58 tests; targeted cleanup, member resume, signed ownership, frozen post heads, dependency fences, missing restore receipt, signature validation, persisted intent validation and delete-proposal guards each fail when weakened. Restored implementation passed 9 selected critical tests. A native dependent-policy warning also reproduced a compensation admission failure; compensation now drops uncommitted success warnings instead of re-emitting rejected content. Its real-SDK regression passes and an isolated function revert is being verified. Starting unchanged-threshold npm and Bun release gates with fresh home and no global Git identity; earlier aggregate coverage and packed runs remain interim evidence."
  "2026-11-06T11:49:21.708Z",codex-sol,"PR 65 is open and queued for CodeRabbit. The first fresh-home full gate passed identity, typecheck, lint, duplication, build and docstrings, then was deliberately stopped during the crash matrix because repeated subprocess V8 collection made each crash case take roughly a minute. That interrupted run is not acceptance evidence. The crash helper now omits V8 output in SIGKILL workers and their retries; every process, boundary and assertion still runs. In-process real-SDK controls measure all authored recovery code; the source inventory and 100/100/100/100 thresholds are unchanged and the full gate will be rerun. Warning-admission revert proof also completed: isolated removal fails; restored code passes."
  "2026-11-06T12:02:23.441Z",codex-sol,"The remaining crash-matrix cost came from reopening native history for every projected version. Inspection now uses the public SDK replayHistoryToTarget plus replayToCanonicalItemDocument with the native schema on the same verified captured stream. No package projection or predicted lifecycle document is introduced. Normal worker V8 collection is restored; source coverage and every subprocess are measured in the final gate. Timeout headroom is increased for complete real-process matrices under shared-host coverage, without removing any case. Two interrupted collector runs remain excluded from acceptance. Focused native-history and peer-preservation controls are being refreshed before the final npm/Bun gates."
  "2026-11-06T12:08:27.729Z",codex-sol,"Focused SDK projection/recovery validation passed 40/40, including one-to-three dependent lost returns and restore progress, process handoff/reclaim, legacy checkpoints, malformed intents, exact signatures, fsync failures, and native warning compensation. Additional disposable behavioral reverts each failed: removing pre-intent settings admission, accepting a peer-corrupted prior ledger, and accepting malformed ledger shape. Restoring all three passed 3/3 selected controls. CodeRabbit started round one against the currently pushed head; the local SDK projection adjustment will be included in the next reviewed push. Starting the final fresh-home full npm gate with normal worker coverage collection and unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-11-06T12:33:58.862Z",codex-sol,"CodeRabbit round one completed on 1adcdd7 with four inline findings and two documentation findings. New real-SDK regressions reproduced reopened committed work, malformed onPrepared refusals, unrelated fsync coupling, and Windows file-handle policy (4/4 failed before changes). A further failing regression exposed compensation restoring an older intent field; discovery now follows the newest non-restore intent in native history so the newer compensation receipt remains replayable. Typed preparation refusals preserve public portable diagnostics and sanitize ordinary errors. Windows file flushes use writable handles; documentation explicitly separates process-crash recovery from unavailable POSIX directory barriers and power-loss claims. Domain reads authenticate proposals once, and compensation visits affected members only. I am checking the native SDK dependency index as a shared conservative candidate selector, rather than copying lifecycle policy. The interrupted pre-review full gate is not acceptance evidence."
  "2026-11-06T13:37:14.185Z",codex-sol,"The independent copied-phase attack reproduced a genuine result-authentication gap: after SIGKILL immediately after the primary native commit, a peer could publish a copied committed phase with invented warnings and obtain false success while the dependent stayed blocked. The new process regression failed before correction. The original fresh invocation now signs the full terminal result, including all post-heads, proposals and warnings; replay and generation retirement verify that signature against the immutable initial public key. New result/review controls pass 9/9. Packed npm and Bun consumers passed 2/2, covering 24 real SIGKILL cases on the declared SDK floor. Current first-push CI failures were a stale native notification assertion and two missing coverage paths; those are addressed and final full gates remain pending."
  "2026-11-06T13:49:01.152Z",codex-sol,"Current pinned-pm execution passed all three linked commands: 8 lifecycle/process tests, 9 result/review tests and 2 targeted peer/notification controls (19 total). Result recording is disabled by project policy, so these counts are recorded here without changing that policy. All nine isolated review reverts fail (10 tests), and the restored implementation passes 10/10. These cover reopened generations, restored older intents, typed preparation errors, Windows file flags and flushes, bounded native dependency admission, unowned retirement, preimage barriers, related-peer preservation and signed terminal-result authentication. Identity, typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication checks pass. Packed npm/Bun recovery passed 2/2 with 24 SIGKILL cases. Full npm/Bun CI and a fresh review are still required on the next pushed head."
  "2026-11-06T14:27:44.115Z",codex-sol,"Both runtime CI suites completed the fix-head functional suite; Node 22 reports 1106/1106 tests passing, with statements/functions/lines at 100 percent and branch coverage at 99.9 percent. No threshold is changed. Three additional native controls cover signed completion with uncleared transfer metadata or stale generation, cross-target copied journals, and an invented untouched post-head member. The frozen-domain control failed before correction: an extra unchanged member was silently ignored. Frozen post-heads now equal the actual changed domain, and the impossible unchanged-member restore continuation is removed. The expanded targeted group passes 17/17; isolated reverts and final full gates are being refreshed."
  "2026-11-06T14:38:41.517Z",codex-sol,"Coverage review found three untested admission branches after 1106 functional CI tests passed. Added six real-SDK boundary cases: copied canonical target, exact affected-member set, and signed ownership cleanup. The affected-set regression failed before the fix. Behavioral reverts of canonical target, cleanup and affected-set guards each fail; the restored six cases pass. Expanded recovery/review/admission tests pass 17/17; pinned pm runner passes the six linked cases. Typecheck, lint, duplication (0%) and docstrings pass. Full npm/Bun gates and the next exact-head bot review remain required."
  "2026-11-06T14:59:11.882Z",codex-sol,"CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/42235851749 passed all 1112 functional tests on Node 26, with statements/functions/lines at 100% and branches at 99.96%. The sole uncovered path is the missing-token side of saved-request normalization. Extended the existing real legacy-native-claim control with a repeated compensated receipt and exact item/history preservation. The local full run was stopped after all 105 SIGKILL child cases passed because the next head needs the added coverage case; it is not full-gate acceptance evidence."
  "2026-11-06T15:01:13.921Z",codex-sol,"The added legacy compensated-receipt retry passes with exact bytes and no duplicate item audit writes, including through the pinned pm test runner. Reverting only completeClaim token normalization makes this control fail 1/1; restored code passes 1/1. Typecheck, lint and duplication (0%) pass. No implementation or coverage threshold changed in this follow-up. Five linked commands now cover 26 tests. Final fresh-home npm/Bun acceptance and current-head CodeRabbit review remain pending; all work items remain open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-06T15:19:40.111Z",codex-sol,"Resumed PR 65 after the orchestrator timeout. The worktree was clean; all three items remain in progress and unclaimed. Current-head CodeRabbit review started. Node 22 CI on d40aef5 passed all 1112 functional tests and the complete 40-source coverage inventory at 100/100/100/100. The npm gate then exposed a packaging assertion: ARCHITECTURE.md was intentionally shipped but absent from the existing artifact allowlist. Correcting that test and verifying real packed npm/Bun consumers. The redundant local full gate was stopped after this authoritative full-coverage CI result; it is not a separate completed gate."
  "2026-11-06T15:34:13.131Z",codex-sol,"Compiled artifact behavioral revert: replacing only completeClaim with the original implementation and rebuilding makes both packed npm and Bun recovery tests fail (0/2 pass). The restored npm control passed; native Bun exceeded the 300-second driver deadline under shared-host load. Increased only these crash-test deadlines (driver 900 seconds, parent 1800), preserving every SIGKILL case and assertion. The corrected artifact allowlist stage passed locally; the unrelated full command-smoke run was stopped after remaining incomplete beyond its deadline, and is not claimed as passing. Fresh CI will verify the complete install gate."
  "2026-11-06T15:41:30.914Z",codex-sol,"Rebuilt compiled-artifact revert proof is complete: the original completeClaim fails both packed npm/Bun recovery tests (0/2), and restoring the function passes both (2/2), covering all 24 SIGKILL cases. Exact command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"recovers every native compensation\" test/install.acceptance.ts. Artifact inventory passes for all 130 files, includes ARCHITECTURE.md and permits no unexpected path. Typecheck, lint and duplication (0%) pass. Prior-head CI proves 1112/1112 functional tests and 100/100/100/100 coverage on all 40 sources. The packaging assertion/deadline correction changes no implementation, case or coverage threshold. Final npm/Bun CI and a current-head bot review remain required at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/pull/65/checks; the queue requested d40aef5 but has not received a bot response yet. Claims are released for orchestrator verification; items stay open."
  "2026-11-06T16:47:28.009Z",codex-sol,"Final target-scope review found a real boundary defect before generation retirement: a valid committed journal copied onto a different owned item was refused at the same token, but accepted as retired when that item had a newer token. The new real-SDK newer-generation control failed with Missing expected rejection, while its same-generation control passed. completeClaim now validates canonical journal target identity immediately after discovery and before any retirement/history certification. A copied receipt cannot authorize a new close on another target. The interim local Bun gate was stopped because this source correction needs fresh exact-head CI; previous green npm gates remain prior-head evidence."
  "2026-11-06T17:07:20.557Z",codex-sol,"The canonical-target correction is verified. The expanded admission suite passes 8/8. Reverting only completeClaim to retirement-before-target validation reproduces the newer-generation failure (1 pass, 2 failures including the parent); omitting the target guard fails all 3 selected tests; restoring it passes 3/3. Fresh pinned-pm execution passes all five linked commands: 8 + 9 + 2 + 8 + 1 = 28 tests. The exact fencing/fair-scheduling command also passes 19/19 on Node 22.18.0 and 19/19 on Node 26.13.0 after this fix. Typecheck, lint and duplication (0%) pass. Prior head f59ad7f now passes both npm/Bun CI and CodeQL, but this final source change requires a fresh exact-head CI run and review. The review queue still has no bot response beyond round one; no current-head approval is claimed. Final evidence remains linked at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/pull/65/checks. All items remain open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-06T20:17:25.788Z",codex-sol,"Resumed review round two on PR 65. All prior code, tests and receipts remain intact. Three new findings require reproduction: null-token committed headers may alter the token, a self-signed fresh intent may claim completion without a core native close, and one rejected dependent-lock release can skip remaining releases. The branch now includes the current dependency baseline from main; its tracked PM history is unchanged. Regression tests will use real non-Git SDK trackers and actual native locks/service overrides. Key consistency alone will not be treated as native close authority; recovery must independently verify the canonical core lifecycle origin before accepting success or related forward mutations."
  "2026-11-06T20:36:22.068Z",codex-sol,Review fixes now require a canonical native primary close before success or dependent compensation; signatures establish consistency only. Null-token committed headers cannot change the prior token. Cleanup attempts every native lease release. One evidence-link write used the configured harness alias codex-agent because the author variable was omitted; this append records codex-sol ownership without rewriting audit history. New regressions use real SDK trackers and a registered service backed by native lock leases.
  "2026-11-06T20:39:24.520Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proofs in disposable copies: removing native-origin checks fails all 4 selected tests (self-signed open/previously-terminal journal cases plus their parent and dependent-compensation control); restoring null-token permissiveness fails 1/1; restoring stop-on-first-release fails 1/1 because only one dependent lease is released. Fixed new suite passes 6/6 with unchanged item/history refusal oracles, legacy successful close/replay, native-lease cleanup and independent OS-process peer writes. Existing admission suite passes 8/8. Typecheck, lint, identity, docstrings and zero-duplication gates pass. Running all six linked commands before final push; CI runs the complete unchanged release gate."
  "2026-11-06T20:45:58.410Z",codex-sol,"Final review-fix validation: all six linked commands pass, 34/34 tests (8+9+2+8+1+6), through pm test --run --progress. Final native-origin revert fails 4/4 selected cases; null-token revert fails 1/1; final cleanup-loop revert fails 1/1 by skipping a retained dependent lease. Fixed 6/6 suite passes, including idempotent retry after cleanup failure and real OS-process peer writes. Final lint and typecheck pass; cleanup collects original recovery failures and every release failure outside finally. Identity, docstrings, zero-duplication and strict isolated pm health pass. PM histories preserve main as an exact byte prefix. Full unchanged npm/Bun release gates and current-head bot review are delegated to the PR pipeline after this combined fix push; no PM item is closed."
  "2026-11-09T10:19:59.899Z",codex-agent,"PR 65 review round: verified both unresolved CodeRabbit threads against the current remote head. Re-read and validate close state after acquiring the operation lease, retain pre-lease committed replay, and tighten the peer-close outcome. Add deterministic non-git tracker race coverage, behavioral revert proofs, and self-review all close/recovery paths for stale state and broad refusal assertions. Latest review has no outside-diff findings."
  "2026-11-09T10:23:27.099Z",codex-agent,"Both findings are valid. Shared request admission and terminal-receipt replay now run again after acquiring the operation lease; fresh callers also refresh the decision document, history and status registry. Added eight real non-git tracker cases: applying-to-committed, two fresh queued closes, completed compensation, four journal identity changes, and changed fencing generation. Self-review found one more broad malformed-journal refusal assertion; each malformed case now requires its exact code, with a separate explicit privacy case. Initial targeted validation passes 12/12. Behavioral revert and error-code mutation proofs are running in the disposable worktree with finally restoration."
  "2026-11-09T10:24:57.101Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for PRRT_kwDOVLY-P860vtEQ: reverting only completeClaim to the reviewed head fails all 8/8 cases in test/close-lease-refresh.test.ts. Restored implementation passes 8/8; the combined changed-file command passes 12/12. Assertion-sensitivity proof for PRRT_kwDOVLY-P860vtEV: substituting swarm_superseded for the pending CloseCompensation outcome fails the tightened peer test (0/1 pass); restoring only the original broad assertion accepts the same wrong result (1/1 pass). Additional malformed-journal sensitivity proof: substituting swarm_private_path at request admission fails the exact-code case (2/3 pass), while reverting only its broad assertion accepts that defect (3/3 pass). All mutations were restored in finally, and the fixed combined suite then passed 12/12. Exact command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/close-lease-refresh.test.ts test/close-peer.test.ts test/close-journal-validation.test.ts. Test-only assertions are proven by mutation sensitivity rather than claiming their reversion changes runtime behavior."
  "2026-11-09T10:26:26.347Z",codex-agent,"Whole-diff self-review also found an unconstrained stale-token rejection in test/close-review.test.ts. It now requires swarm_stale_fence. Sensitivity proof: changing only StaleFenceError.code to swarm_superseded fails the selected test (0/1), restoring only the original unconstrained assertion accepts it (1/1), then restoring the implementation and tightened assertion passes (1/1). Typecheck, lint, docstrings (40 sources, 214 declarations) and unchanged zero-duplication gate pass. The initial linked runner refused six inherited commands because this disposable branch has a different provenance ref; after inspecting the commands, local trust was acknowledged separately without changing stored provenance or execution policy. All seven linked commands are being rerun."
  "2026-11-09T10:27:49.865Z",codex-agent,"Final linked targeted run passes all seven commands (46/46 tests: 8+9+2+8+1+6+12), including every changed test file and the prior blocking cases. Strict isolated self-host health passes all 10 checks; one existing advisory telemetry queue remains, without changing telemetry configuration. Main history prefix verification passes for all three PR history streams. Dist is ignored and has no committed files; the full release gate rebuilds it for packed acceptance. Starting sequential npm and Bun release gates with fresh HOME, disabled global Git configuration and inherited credentials removed; all thresholds stay unchanged."
  "2026-11-09T11:04:42.587Z",codex-agent,"Final release validation: credential-stripped isolated-HOME npm run release:check passes in 2120 seconds (35m20s). Functional suite: 1128/1128, zero failures/skips/cancellations, including all 105 SIGKILL boundaries. Coverage: 40 measured sources at 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines; unchanged thresholds. Packed acceptance: 7/7, including real npm/npx, native Bun/bunx, fresh non-git trackers, shared global-host artifact and 24 packed crash-recovery cases. Identity, typecheck, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, production audit, package inventory, canonical changelog and publish attestation all pass. The subsequent bun run release:check passed identity/typecheck/lint/duplication/build/docstrings and was deliberately stopped during its duplicate coverage suite: the measured npm runtime predicts both full runs exceed the requested about-60-minute host budget. Signal-induced cancellations from that stop are not a completed Bun gate or a product-test failure. Full Bun certification remains for final-head CI. No local timeout or assertion failure occurred in the completed npm gate."
  "2026-11-09T11:04:45.472Z",codex-agent,"Review-round completion: PRRT_kwDOVLY-P860vtEQ is fixed by shared initial/lease-held request admission and journal/receipt refresh in src/close.ts; its eight regression cases fail on completeClaim-only revert. PRRT_kwDOVLY-P860vtEV now requires swarm_compensation_partial in test/close-peer.test.ts; the recorded error-code mutant is caught only by the tightened assertion. Whole-diff self-review also tightened malformed-journal and stale-token outcomes, with recorded sensitivity proofs. No finding was refused as invalid. Latest review contains no outside-diff findings. Final implementation and tracker history are retained for orchestrator verification; no threads were answered or resolved, and no item is closed. Full Bun release CI remains outstanding; strict health has only the pre-existing advisory telemetry queue. No PM CLI/SDK defect was discovered in this round."
  "2026-11-09T11:06:00.853Z",codex-agent,"Final staged verification after all review-round changes: identity reports 0 violations, canonical changelog check passes, strict isolated health passes 10/10 with 0 warnings (the earlier advisory queue cleared without configuration changes), and all three PR history streams preserve main as a byte-identical prefix. Fresh fetch confirms the PR branch and main have not advanced during validation. Eight explicit changed paths contain code, regression tests, docs and this append-only tracker evidence; no distribution or binary artifacts are tracked. Final-head CI will be visible at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/pull/65/checks. The item remains in_progress and my claim is released for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-09T13:13:08.949Z",codex-agent,"Continuing PR #65 at its remote head; main is already an ancestor. Thread PRRT_kwDOVLY-P861QrQN is valid. General rule: a failed confirmation read is not positive authorization to compensate; durable committed intents must never transition back into compensation. Auditing all compensation entry points and shared SDK/CLI render paths, including packed Node/Bun and non-Git trackers. Will centralize native intent reconciliation before rollback and add adversarial failure/retry coverage without replacing native SDK mutations."
  "2026-11-09T13:20:00.637Z",codex-agent,"Class fix: all compensation callers now rediscover the authoritative native intent, preserve missing/replaced intent, refuse a committed receipt as swarm_partial_commit, and check the inspected primary head before the first rollback write. Removed both forced applying fallbacks from applyClose. The package-wide search found no other rollback writer: SDK SharedTracker/Swarm and CLI JSON/TOON all delegate here. New adversarial matrix covers final native-sync failure, lost response, one-shot item/history read failure, stale phases, missing/replaced intent, and a commit between discovery and inspection on real non-Git trackers. Revert proof in a disposable worktree: restoring only src/close-recovery.ts to the prior implementation makes all 7/7 new tests fail (exit 1), including audit/intent corruption; the fixed tests pass in the focused run. Packed acceptance now also checks 0/1/3-dependent lost confirmations and write-free SDK/JSON/TOON replay for both npm/Node and native Bun consumers."
  "2026-11-09T13:23:58.375Z",codex-agent,"Final focused evidence: 38/38 close recovery tests passed; final linked regression command passes 7/7 with exact swarm_partial_commit assertions. The packed npm/Node and native Bun targeted acceptance passes 2/2 (24 total SIGKILL cases and 12 lost-confirmation cases across 0/1/3 dependents, plus write-free SDK/JSON/TOON replay). Final-code behavioral revert: prior src/close-recovery.ts causes 0/7 pass; removing only the inspected-primary committed guard causes 0/1 pass in the discovery/inspection race. Clarification of the package-wide audit: close recovery is the only native restore writer; claim, resource and Git cleanup paths already require acquisitionSnapshot/history guards and do not convert read failures into rollback authorization. All 3 changed native history streams retain main as a byte prefix. Typecheck, lint, zero-duplication, docstring, identity and changelog checks pass. Starting sequential credential-free isolated-HOME npm and Bun release gates with at most two test workers."
  "2026-11-09T13:50:26.853Z",codex-agent,"Additional class audit hardened rediscovery against plan substitution: both recovery entry and refusal-summary rediscovery now use the SAME exported closePlanIdentity as native history inspection, preserving protocol, compensation identity, target, author, token, note, members and signing key. A matching compensation identifier alone is insufficient. Added seven field-substitution variants on fresh real trackers. Final focused command (close-commit-confirmation, close-journal-validation, close-proof-boundaries, close-lease-refresh and close-recovery) passes 49/49. The 15-case linked regression command passes. Prior recovery-function revert fails seven tests; inspected-head guard revert fails its race test; identifier-only rediscovery mutant fails five substitution variants (six failures including the parent test). Stopped the superseded full npm gate after the additional identity hardening; its cancellations are not certification. Final typecheck/lint/docstring and 0 percent duplication checks pass. Restarting complete npm and Bun release checks sequentially on the final implementation."
