  "2026-11-10T09:29:35.465Z",codex-agent,"Round 5 npm run release:check PASSED on source commit 4f6c06a in 2111 seconds (35m11s), with credential-free isolated HOME/Git configuration and at most two workers. Source suite 1195/1195 and installed consumers 7/7, zero failures/skips/cancellations; all 42 authored sources measure unchanged 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. Identity 0 violations; typecheck, lint, duplication 0 percent, docstrings, production audit 0 vulnerabilities, npm pack dry-run, changelog and release attestation all pass. Installed npm/npx, native Bun/bunx, fresh non-Git trackers, shared/separate host SDKs, Git ownership and packed crash recovery all passed using artifact SHA1 281952fee73f29a79b2d220566f94eae1ded8af6. Fresh disposable-clone strict pm health exits 0 with only stale_in_progress_items:2 advisory. Focused linked command also passed 88/88 through pinned pm test --only-last --run --progress. The separate previous Node 26 CI reporter heap limit is tracked by follow-up pm-swarm-9bks; no duplicate PR or correctness item was opened. Starting sequential Bun full release gate."
  "2026-11-10T09:29:57.017Z",codex-agent,"Changed fleet acceptance file also passes directly: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/privacy-fleet.acceptance.ts, with PUBLIC_FLEET_ROOT pointing to a disposable synthetic corpus (one Git repository, one genuine non-Git directory). Result 1/1; three tracked relative paths, 27 prose/Markdown presentations, parentheses/brackets/slot/space path shapes, zero false refusals, one correctly skipped non-repository and zero source writes. No private repository was read for this corpus."
  "2026-11-10T10:09:49.289Z",codex-agent,"Round 5 FINAL verification on implementation commit 4f6c06a: npm run release:check exits 0 in 2111s (35m11s), and bun run release:check exits 0 in 2331s (38m51s). EACH complete isolated command passes 1195/1195 source tests and 7/7 installed consumers, zero failures/skips/cancellations; EACH measures all 42 authored sources at unchanged 100/100/100/100 coverage. Local runtimes Node 24.19.0 and Bun 1.3.5. Both consume artifact SHA1 281952fee73f29a79b2d220566f94eae1ded8af6. Full identity, typecheck, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, production audit, pack, changelog and release attestation all pass. Focused six-file command passes 88/88 through pinned pm test --only-last --run --progress; synthetic fleet acceptance passes 1/1. Four isolated behavioral reverts exit 1; restored regressions pass 5/5. Thread mapping to 4f6c06a: PRRT_kwDOVLY-P861nnJY -> accurate coverage timeout budget, test/review-round-five.test.ts coverage timeout; PRRT_kwDOVLY-P861nnJl -> upward whole-millisecond deadline, test/linked-test-deadline.test.ts fractional property; PRRT_kwDOVLY-P861nnJ3 -> null recovery-version refusal before intent writes, test/review-round-five.test.ts primary/dependent checkpoint races; PRRT_kwDOVLY-P861nnKP -> fail-closed complete fleet inventory, test/review-round-five.test.ts unsuccessful probes. The older open PRRT_kwDOVLY-P861kjmp is already fixed by dd19529 with test/review-probe-failures.test.ts. All four new findings valid and fixed; none declined. Main remains unchanged and an ancestor. Releasing only this claim; item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification. No threads replied to, resolved or reacted to; no merge or release. Prior Node 26 CI reporter heap exhaustion remains separate follow-up pm-swarm-9bks. Fresh pushed-head CI/re-review remains required at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/pull/65/checks. No new pm CLI/SDK defect found."
  "2026-11-10T10:27:50.047Z",codex-agent,"Auto round 6 continuation: preserved remote head 323f7ee and reused its clean continuation worktree; origin/main is already an ancestor. Three unresolved threads are valid. General rules: recovery advice must distinguish parseable pending intent from malformed intent; native SDK/CLI subprocess deadlines must allow suite budgets; fixed regex patterns must not be reconstructed per visited AST node. Package scan found the same misleading advice in reclaim receipts (SDK and both output encodings) and two more 10-second native CLI children in acquisition-generations. Will correct all, add adversarial contract checks and behavioral recovery assertions, prove reverts in disposable copies, run focused then sequential full npm/Bun gates with two workers, and release this claim without closing the item."
  "2026-11-10T10:33:30.495Z",codex-agent,"Round 6 class fixes and revert proofs: recovery instructions distinguish valid pending retry from malformed explicit inspection. Reclaim now forwards the authoritative admission refusal instead of replacing it with combined advice, covering SDK, JSON/TOON, preview/apply, pool/receiver, Git-free trackers and packed npm/Bun consumers. The malformed original request itself refuses without changing native bytes. General timeout scan found three 10-second SDK/CLI invocations (confirmation plus two acquisition peers) and the 20-second installed watch child; all now allow 120 seconds, preserving their surrounding workflow barriers and intentional 25ms idle-child timeout fault injection. New AST budget inventory covers all seven APIs, member spellings and copied APIs with an independent boundary corpus (1/25/10000/20000/29999 refuse, 30000/120000/300000 allow). Existing embedded-program deadline inventory still covers packed drivers. Fixed child-call regex is now a module literal; all other package regex constructors were inspected: production patterns already compile at module scope and test-only variable patterns represent changing expected values, rather than a fixed visitor pattern. Six disposable-copy behavioral reverts each exited 1 with assertion failures: native guide, reclaim message forwarding, confirmation timeout, acquisition timeouts, installed watch timeout, and visitor regex construction. Restored proof command passes 5/5; the focused five-file command passes 109/109 through pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress. Initial focused run caught the old broad close-intent wording assertion; it now requires the more precise interrupted-episode retry message. Typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication pass; no tests or thresholds weakened. Full isolated npm/Bun release gates follow sequentially with two workers."
  "2026-11-10T10:36:01.312Z",codex-agent,"Final documentation class cross-check also corrected README.md, ARCHITECTURE.md and both active companion recovery guides: each now distinguishes a valid pending retry from malformed intent inspection, and the shared recovery-guide contract checks every guide plus the README and state table. Ten isolated reverts now fail with assertions (five documentation surfaces, reclaim advice, confirmation deadline, acquisition deadlines, installed watch deadline and regex construction); restoring all files passes the five selected proof regressions. The final contract/budget focused command passes 9/9; lint and typecheck pass. The first npm gate was intentionally stopped early to include this complete documentation class fix; both complete release gates will restart on the final committed source. No raw pi transcript was read; prior valid work and all audit records are retained."
  "2026-11-10T11:23:59.921Z",codex-agent,"Round 6 npm release invocation completed in 2651s with exit 1 solely in installed global-host setup: npm registry ETIMEDOUT fetching the pinned public host tarball. All 1198/1198 source tests passed; 42 authored sources remain 100/100/100/100; identity, typecheck, lint, zero duplication, build, docstrings, production audit (0 vulnerabilities), pack, changelog and publication attestation passed. Installed consumers passed 6/7, including BOTH packed crash-recovery matrices with the new pending-versus-malformed advice assertions and fresh npm/Bun non-Git command runs. Artifact SHA1 2fea8e55334e9dccb58e6c230f2205c6db727938. The unchanged global-host focused retry also failed with registry metadata ETIMEDOUT (81s), before product behavior. No test, dependency or threshold workaround applied. Strict prepared-clone self-host health exits 0 with only stale_in_progress_items:2 advisory. The separate full Bun release gate remains required and will run sequentially; the initial nonzero npm invocation remains explicit evidence."
  "2026-11-10T11:28:12.028Z",codex-agent,"Registry verification: public metadata and pinned-tarball HEAD requests each returned HTTP 200, but a second unchanged isolated global-host retry still failed before product execution with npm metadata ETIMEDOUT in 81s. Thus there are three preserved network-failure receipts (full npm invocation plus two focused attempts), not a green npm release claim. Remote refs refreshed: main remains an ancestor and the PR branch has not changed. Starting the required separate full Bun gate sequentially, with the same source, thresholds and two-worker budget."
  "2026-11-10T12:15:13.766Z",codex-agent,"Round 6 FINAL source verification: implementation commits a235dcc and 1b3842b fix all three valid threads at class scope; d561b3f preserves interim network receipts. Thread mapping: PRRT_kwDOVLY-P861pwOg -> a235dcc plus 1b3842b (valid pending retry versus malformed explicit inspection throughout native guide, README, state table, both companion guides and authoritative SDK/JSON/TOON reclaim advice); PRRT_kwDOVLY-P861pwOl -> a235dcc (all discovered short peer/installed-watch deadlines, adversarial package API/alias budget inventory); PRRT_kwDOVLY-P861pwO0 -> a235dcc (one fixed module regex literal, repeated-match/API/AST contracts). No findings declined, and no review thread was answered or resolved. Ten independent disposable-copy reverts fail with assertions; restored selected regressions pass 5/5. Revert-sensitive commands: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='active recovery guides' test/review-close-contracts.test.ts; node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='every transfer surface preserves a malformed' test/close-transfer-process.test.ts; node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='every package peer deadline' test/review-peer-budgets.test.ts; node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='deadline visitor uses fixed' test/review-close-contracts.test.ts. Focused five-file linked command passes 109/109; final strengthened contracts/budgets pass 9/9. Both isolated npm run release:check (2651s) and bun run release:check (2594s) pass 1198/1198 source tests and unchanged 100/100/100/100 coverage over all 42 authored sources, plus identity/typecheck/lint/zero duplication/build/docstrings/production audit/pack/changelog/attestation. Both full commands EXIT 1 at installed setup: npm consumers 6/7 (global-host registry ETIMEDOUT); Bun consumers 3/7 (two ETIMEDOUT and two ERESOLVE reports showing an undefined host version during npm installation). The declared floor 2026.10.23 satisf